# Tests before every commit

`yarn test` runs before every commit. The Husky `pre-commit` hook is what blocks the commit. Do not commit when the suite is red, and do not skip the hook.

A new feature ships with a unit test in the same change. A new feature is a new reply, status, or security decision of a slash command, Discord or Lavalink event, Bot API handler, Dashboard action, background job, or helper. Add one `*.test.ts` under `tests/`, mirroring the source path, for each distinct outcome. Dashboard tests go in `tests/web/`. Do not place tests next to production files.

A change to an existing feature, a bug fix, or a security fix adds or updates the test that asserts the changed reply, status, or security decision. That assertion would have failed on the old behavior. A refactor that does not change a reply, status, or security decision does not require a test edit.

React components and thin `app/api` proxies are not features under this rule. Dashboard tests stay unit tests of `server/`, `lib/`, and shared helpers.
